{
  "name": "it-ontology",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "description": "IT ontology, first version. One subject taxonomy, four orthogonal dimensions: TOGAF supplies the structure dimension (what the IT landscape is), SCAP the identity dimension (how subjects are named and configured), ISO 25000 the quality dimension (how well subjects perform), and W3C PROV the provenance dimension (who bears responsibility and whence things derive). Dimensions are articulated by typed axes; concept identity across dimensions is captured by correspondences. Concepts are referenced by title - globally unambiguous under the catalogue's framework-prefix naming rule - and resolved to $id through the dimension registry. Schema-level composition (allOf facets) remains a per-need decision at this domain layer; ItSoftwareTechnology is the executed exemplar.",
